Background: rebuild_reason_pinset in src/main.rs:2176-2195 allocates two new Vecs per call:

    let mut pinned_clauses = Vec::new();
    let mut pinned_binaries = Vec::new();
    for &reason in &self.reason {
        match reason.as_ref_unchecked() {
            ReasonRef::Clause(clause_idx) => pinned_clauses.push(clause_idx),
            ReasonRef::Binary(binary_id) => pinned_binaries.push(binary_id),
            ReasonRef::None => {}
        }
    }
    pinned_clauses.sort_unstable();
    pinned_clauses.dedup();
    pinned_binaries.sort_unstable_by_key(|binary_id| binary_id.0);
    pinned_binaries.dedup_by_key(|binary_id| binary_id.0);

The function is called from reduce_db_with_proof and from GC code paths. Plan section 2 invariant: "propagation, conflict analysis, decision selection, and reduce-db candidate scans do not allocate in steady state." This violates that invariant on the reduce-db side. On large instances with deep trails, the Vecs grow from zero capacity through multiple reallocations to fit the assigned-variable count.

Goal: add scratch fields scratch_pinned_clauses: Vec<ClauseRef> and scratch_pinned_binaries: Vec<BinaryClauseId> to Solver. rebuild_reason_pinset clears them at entry, populates, sorts, dedups in-place. The returned ReasonPinSet can either continue to own its Vecs (via std::mem::take from the scratch fields at the end), or the API can change to accept &mut ReasonPinSet from the caller — pick the cleaner option.

Implementation notes:
- The existing ReasonPinSet { pinned_clauses, pinned_binaries, generation } struct can be moved to a single owned-by-Solver scratch ReasonPinSet field; reduce_db and GC borrow it by &self.
- Verify no caller holds a long-lived ReasonPinSet beyond the reduce-db / GC call (the plan section 1.3 says ReasonPinSet must be rebuilt fresh per reduce/GC pass).
- Add a counter reason_pinset_rebuilds and surface in trace_full to confirm the no-allocation path is hit.

Tests:
- test_rebuild_reason_pinset_no_allocation (use a tracking allocator under cfg(test))
- test_rebuild_reason_pinset_clears_previous_contents
- test_rebuild_reason_pinset_handles_zero_assigned_vars
- existing reduce-DB and GC tests must pass unchanged

Benchmark gate: search-core + discriminating on UNSAT-heavy instances that trigger frequent reduce-DB calls (REGRandom K4, SCPC-500). Counters: reduce_db_calls, gc_count, allocator pressure proxy (hot_allocations_estimated if it captures this site). Expected: no PAR-2 regression; lower steady-state allocator pressure.

